+## 9. Fifth build, 2026-09-16 04:10Z to 05:00Z: things of parts, on A1's colour eye, inside the clock
+
+Joe: "a ball with a pattern is not a bear"; and, of the plan to leave it so, "a new low line". Built:
+
+- **Parts.** `ObjectPart(kind, offset, size, paint)`: a box, a sphere or a vertical cylinder in the thing's own frame; a thing of shape "parts" carries one to sixteen of them; the footprint disc must cover every part's plan below the walking layer; in the record only for such things. Thirty-one things of her home are parts now (118 parts): the bear (body, head, two ears, a muzzle, four limbs), the apple with its stem, the cup with its handle, bowl, pot and pan with handles, chairs with seats, backs and legs, tables and the desk with tops and legs, the bed with mattress, headboard and legs, the sofa with arms, the armchair, the television on its stand, shelves with four boards, the refrigerator with its handle, the stove with its rings, the pantry, the tub, the basin on its stem, the trees with trunks and canopies, the swing, the slide, the radio with its aerial, the floor lamp's base and stand.
+- **The eye meets them part by part** (`w1_parts.py`): every ray against every part of the things in the room (slab test, quadratic, circle and caps), the nearest wins, with its true normal and its paint; only the rays that enter a thing's bounding sphere are cast against its parts. A thing of parts shadows part by part (a ray's own part never shadows it; its other parts do). Spheres and boxes stand in front of and behind parts by depth.
+- **On A1's eye.** A1 made the focal field 160 × 120 at 0.375° a site and three channels (red = bands 0 and 1, green = 2 and 3, blue = 4 and 5; 58,005 values a beat) with a colour figure law, commit 42ff72dd5; the parts law was rebased on it and the rendering function is C1's from here.
+- **Inside the clock.** With the colour eye and the parts her beat was 303 ms median. Two costs, neither geometry: A1's per-pixel conversion of nineteen thousand exact fractions (now one array: `np.array(pixels)`, the three channels vectorized) and the world re-encoding two megabytes of receipts as canonical JSON on every action (sixteen retained receipts of a 52-thing home; now four, a world recorded with sixteen restores keeping its latest four under the authenticated migration). Measured after: 221 ms median, 257 p90, 364 worst on 120 beats by day; the live world (66 things, 16 receipts) restores in 3.5 s and re-restores exactly.
+
+A bear from a metre away, in colour: a brown body and head, two ears, a dark muzzle, on the plank floor, its shadow on the wall behind.
